; BushCommon — Forest terrain variant: ground-level UNDERGROWTH, not a tree. Keeps the
; "some variety, which is why I like the Bushes" read the human asked for, in the MegaKit's own
; style rather than the Ultimate Nature Pack Bush/BushBerries this replaces.
;
; NOT the flowering sibling (Bush_Common_Flowers), deliberately: `flowers` is Meadow's habitat
; tag and Meadow is its only source, so flowering shrubs stay off every other terrain. Same call
; already applied to Scrub — see scrub.tres's header.
;
; SHARED WITH SCRUB, AT THE SAME SIZE. Scrub instances this identical mesh at 0.37932, and this
; wrapper matches it exactly so one mesh is never two heights in one world. That is not a
; collision: Scrub pairs it with a dry olive/tan slab and browse props, so the shared shrub sits
; in an unmistakably different tile.
;
; SCALE: raw mesh AABB height 1.581786 -> scaled 0.37932 for the ~0.6 tile-unit ground-level
; shrub class Bush.tscn established, well under every tree.
;
; STANDARDISED ONTO THE STYLIZED NATURE MEGAKIT (2026-09-08, human ruling: "make sure all of our
; trees used the same Stylized Nature Megakit"). Forest previously drew from three packs at once;
; the MegaKit is the one that also supplies the GROUND these trees stand on (grass.tres,
; meadow.tres, wild_grass.tres all draw from it), which is the adjacency that reads hardest, so
; it is the pack the whole terrain now uses. Source: Stylized Nature MegaKit (Standard/free),
; Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — License.txt re-checked per asset-import-pipeline.md's audit
; gate. See project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; SLAB AND FLOOR PATCHES ARE COPIED VERBATIM FROM CommonTree1.tscn — same forest green
; Color(0.16, 0.4, 0.22), same 1.0 x 0.2 x 1.0 geometry (the 1.0 width is the established
; cross-tile seam-gap fix, do not narrow it), same 3 moss/leaf-litter PlaneMesh patches at
; y=0.001. Deliberately not a new taste call: every Forest variant shares one floor so the
; terrain reads as one thing while the silhouettes differ.
;
; EVERYTHING GROUND-LEVEL NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" — the OcclusionFader exemption
; convention; see CommonTree1.tscn's header for the mechanism.
;
; SCALE IS MEASURED, NOT GUESSED, but the TARGET is still a first-pass judgment call inherited
; from CommonTree1.tscn (there is no GDD number for tree height) — FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF.
;
; OCCLUSIONFADER REMOVED 2026-09-08 — ANY MENTION OF IT BELOW IS HISTORY. The per-resident
; transparency fade (D-41 §4) flickered in play and was cut outright; the script, its scene node
; and its two suites are gone. The "Slab" node stays, because every terrain scene is built
; around it and removing it would restructure all 33 for no gain — but NO CODE LOOKS THAT NAME
; UP ANY MORE. It is a grouping convention now, with no behaviour attached, so nothing breaks if
; a new scene groups differently and nothing is gained by "restoring" the exemption.
[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

